# Secure Log Aggregation Setup – AWS DevOps Lab

## Project Overview

This project implements a secure, automated log aggregation pipeline using AWS infrastructure. It transfers system logs from a private EC2 instance to a public EC2 instance and then uploads them to a private Amazon S3 bucket.

The solution uses VPC peering for private network communication, IAM roles for controlled S3 access, SSH for log transfer, and cron jobs for automation.

## Objectives

- Configure private and public VPC environments.
- Establish secure communication through VPC peering.
- Deploy EC2 instances in separate VPCs.
- Configure an IAM role with restricted S3 upload permissions.
- Automate log transfer from the private EC2 instance.
- Automatically upload collected logs to Amazon S3.
- Verify the uploaded log object and encryption.

